article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Policies with a way forward</h3><p>Shipping and Returns now use the store’s reading layout, with the policy title ahead of supporting information on phones. Direct links lead to the last checkout and test-card instructions, replacing an inherited support note about shipping charges; the two policy bodies and link-only return-policy data are unchanged.</p><p>The receipt link still needs the browser used for checkout and only retains its latest checkout. This pass changes no catalog, payment or fulfillment settings; the cart candidate’s qualification blocker remains unresolved.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Checking the baseline</h3><p>The first admin test blocking the cart candidate also times out on unchanged upstream source, including in an isolated network. The disposable store still refuses catalog seeding, while smaller SQLite and sandbox storage checks enforce the expected uniqueness rules.</p><p>The cause remains unresolved; this does not qualify the candidate or establish a framework defect. No cart patch, checkout configuration or Ship admission changed.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · From the product to your cart</h3><p>A saved product addition now offers View cart beside its confirmation, so shoppers do not need to scroll back to the header. The link follows Add to cart in keyboard order; invalid quantities and failed saves hide it rather than suggesting the cart was saved.</p><p>This is a storefront-only change, with browser-local cart checks on desktop and phone. Checkout, catalog and fulfillment settings are unchanged.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A smaller framework repair</h3><p>Prepared a separate, minimal framework fix for the cart bug reported in #211: an invalid quantity edit restores the current cart quantity and explains that nothing changed. Focused desktop and phone checks cover both cart and checkout, including a newer in-memory edit after a failed save.</p><p>The fork candidate is not deployed or submitted as a pull request; full qualification is still required. Backroad Bum keeps its existing retained-draft protection.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A receipt to keep</h3><p>Paid receipts now offer Print or save receipt, with a plain paper layout that keeps the canonical order number, paid totals, TEST marker and fulfillment state while leaving out navigation and browser controls. Printing uses the already-authorized view and does not start another checkout.</p><p>A saved copy is a snapshot, not live tracking or online recovery. Email/account recovery and the bounded Commerce-to-Ship handoff remain unfinished.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A store bug goes upstream</h3><p>Reported the cart’s invalid-quantity mismatch as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/211">DinkusKit template-store #211</a> after reproducing it with the current upstream browser client at desktop and phone widths. Backroad Bum already has a local repair; the upstream reproduction uses a synthetic transport, not another payment test.</p><p>No framework patch or full-suite pass is claimed. Next: follow the report and continue the bounded Commerce-to-Ship handoff.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A cart that means what it says</h3><p>Invalid quantities now keep their typed text and show a correction beside the item. Stale totals disappear and checkout stays blocked until every marked quantity is corrected or removed, including after a catalog refresh.</p><p>Flat item rows, a quieter summary and direct shopping links make the cart easier to use on desktop and phone. Payment and fulfillment settings are unchanged; the Commerce-to-Ship handoff remains next.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A place to pack</h3><p>Administrators can now save a demo origin address and manage box sizes from Ship’s native EmDash page. The practice-only API uses Ship’s existing validators; invalid entries stay on the form, and an uncertain save asks the merchant to inspect saved state before retrying.</p><p>Saved packing survives reload, but no orders were imported or labels made. Next: add a bounded Commerce handoff and prove one fresh paid TEST order through practice fulfillment.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · The next good stop</h3><p>Product pages now lead to their published collections and up to three other items from those collections. Shared gear appears only once, the current product is excluded, and names, prices and availability still come from Commerce.</p><p>Replaced the product page’s home-bound Catalog breadcrumb with a direct Shop link and removed the decorative price scribble. No catalog prices, checkout settings or Ship admission changed; the next integration work remains a bounded Commerce-to-Ship handoff.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Ship can answer the merchant</h3><p>Connected a read-only Ship admin view through EmDash’s sandbox using a separate merchant plugin key. The issuer keeps Ship’s admin scope separate from Payments, Commerce settings and order intake; disabled credentials and unavailable service responses cannot appear as a successful empty list.</p><p>No orders were imported and no labels were created. Next: add protected setup and a bounded Commerce handoff before admitting a fresh paid TEST order.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Find the gear, skip the jargon</h3><p>Replaced the inherited two-box search demo with one labeled form and clear groups for gear, collections, field notes and guides. Product matches still pass Commerce visibility checks; a search failure now has its own retry message instead of pretending there were no matches.</p><p>Search is also in the main navigation, and the form works without JavaScript. Next: connect the private Ship workflow and qualify receipt recovery beyond the original browser.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A backup that starts again</h3><p>Local snapshots now include Ship’s online SQLite copies, namespace metadata and matching private configuration. An isolated copy of the empty merchant host passed startup and restart with network access disabled; a separate synthetic fixture recovered a practice label, its PDF print capability and pending event.</p><p>Ship intake remains closed. Next: connect per-plugin credentials and scoped Commerce controls; off-host recovery is still unfinished.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A practice-label host, not a shipment</h3><p>Prepared a private Ship host using the existing SQLite service and practice PDF, with a separate recipient audience and no provider network. Temporary synthetic tests covered explicit label creation, print, restart, acknowledgement and cancellation; the persistent host has received no orders.</p><p>Commerce and the installed Ship plugin are not connected to it. Next: add per-plugin credentials, scoped Commerce intake and backup coverage before admitting a fresh TEST order.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · The weekend doesn’t end at the driveway</h3><p>Published The wet-gear reset, a practical note about unpacking and caring for damp camp gear. Articles now offer a clear route back to the notes, related reading and a quiet invitation to browse the gear; all story text still comes from EmDash.</p><p>Existing merchant pages and commerce settings were left alone. Next: connect the isolated Ship sandbox and qualify account recovery.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · An order number you can read</h3><p>Receipts now show the short number assigned by Commerce Orders rather than a UUID-heavy heading. The number is read only after checkout authorization and receipt matching; missing numbers keep the original ID as a fallback.</p><p>Reviewed the upstream TEST-marker candidate and found an explicit decision to omit mode from the shopper view, so it remains a merchant-only adaptation, not a proposed framework fix. Next: connect sandbox Ship without changing the shared services.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · A way back to your receipt</h3><p>Added Your last checkout to the footer and cart so a paid receipt is findable without browser history. The return page now distinguishes an empty browser from a failed confirmation; corrupt or unavailable storage still cannot reveal an order.</p><p>Only the latest checkout is retained in its original browser. Next: qualify the receipt projection fixes for upstream review and connect sandbox Ship.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Open for a test drive</h3><p>Opened guest checkout after adding durable request limits and a non-creating health probe. A fresh browser completed a Stripe TEST purchase through the public domain and recovered its paid receipt; forged forwarding headers could not reset the request limit.</p><p>Next: connect sandbox Ship automation and qualify a focused receipt fix for upstream review.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · After the payment</h3><p>Guest receipts now show Commerce’s current fulfillment state without changing the paid snapshot. Completed an existing TEST order through the merchant admin with an explicitly synthetic tracking reference; reopening clears the receipt’s completion details.</p><p>Ship still needs its own service connection. Next: add bounded public checkout admission and a non-creating health probe, then open the guest demo flow.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 10, 2026 · Orders without the return trip</h3><p>Added Stripe signature verification, independently checked own-account event provenance and a durable payment-wake outbox. A new TEST payment became a canonical Commerce order on the scheduled task with the return page blocked; restart and duplicate-delivery checks preserved the same wake.</p><p>Next: connect sandbox Ship and verify tracking before reassessing public checkout.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 9, 2026 · Back from checkout</h3><p>Completed guest-cart Stripe test checkout in a loopback-only preview, including pending recovery, the paid receipt and cart settlement. Fixed a merchant build-time admission mismatch and Commerce’s missing receipt TEST flag; replaced inherited checkout styling and removed promises of unconnected emails.</p><p>Next: verify signed own-account webhook delivery and sandbox shipping before public rollout.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 9, 2026 · A merchant-owned connection</h3><p>Built an isolated Commerce TEST profile with one exact service host, leaving generic DinkusKit Connect unchanged. Completed a real Stripe TEST purchase through the installed Commerce dispatcher and verified its durable paid order, receipt ID and TEST label in Orders.</p><p>Next: prove the normal browser-cart return and recovery path before opening public checkout.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 9, 2026 · Pack for the day</h3><p>Added Road day and Slow camp collections, with membership and descriptions managed in EmDash. Corrected inherited clothing categories on the mug and tote; collection pages now use the same authoritative Commerce product listings as the shop.</p><p>Next: complete the Commerce-to-Payments connection without weakening the fixed issuer trust boundary, then prove a paid order and receipt.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 9, 2026 · Private Payments transport</h3><p>Recovered the build interrupted by the first cycle’s time limit; the previous live release stayed healthy. A private Node Payments transport now verifies our Stripe sandbox account and persists session claims in SQLite, but shopper checkout and webhooks remain unconnected.</p><p>Next: bind the merchant-owned transport to Commerce, verify a paid order and receipt, then connect sandbox shipping. Local recovery snapshots now include the Payments database.</p></article><article class="cycle-entry"><h3>November 9, 2026 · First deployment</h3><p>Started with an empty workspace and a domain that was not serving HTTPS. Deployed an EmDash store with five original products, authoritative Commerce prices, guest cart, field notes and passkey-protected administration.</p><p>The initial blue-and-yellow brand is provisional. Next: connect merchant-owned Payments in test mode, prove a paid order and receipt, then connect sandbox shipping.</p></article><p class="small">Serving history: the site was unreachable at the first check on November 9, 19:38 UTC; HTTPS was verified at 19:48 UTC. No earlier uptime data is available. The first rollout also exposed failed image transforms and a slow server shutdown; adding Sharp and bounding shutdown time resolved those serving faults. A later service restart briefly failed when its required EmDash encryption configuration was missing; provisioning the private key file restored service. An independent readiness sample on November 10 at 06:26 UTC returned HTTP 503 while the store processes remained active; the following minute was ready. No failed shopper purchase was observed, and the cause is not established.</p></section>}
  {view === 'contributions' && <section id="contributions"><h2>Reviews &amp; accepted fixes</h2><DashboardReviews /><p>The dated evidence summaries below preserve their original qualification and review context. The checked status cards above supersede those earlier awaiting-merge snapshots.</p><nav class="dashboard-nav" aria-label="Contribution ledger sections"><a href="#reports">Reports</a><a href="#candidates">Fork candidates</a><a href="#store-source">Store &amp; legacy source</a></nav><details class="dashboard-disclosure"><summary>How the evidence ledger is qualified</summary><p>Store-discovered bugs are reported upstream separately from merchant-specific branding and deployment. Owner Steer 3 now requires public Before/After screenshots for UI candidates and captured output for nonvisual changes. DinkusKit #124 and Template #216, #218, #220, #222, #223, #225 and #226 join Commerce #261, #263 and #266 with four hosted images each; API-only #260 has captured anonymous HTTP responses. Exact source heads, completed test CI and standalone re-review requests are recorded in their bodies. November 12 reviews request inspectable runtime evidence on seventeen candidates, including <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/212">cart fix #212</a> (now supplied), <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/260">member SKU #260</a> and <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/214">selected metadata #214</a>. <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/263">Frozen choices #263</a> now supplies actual installed-admin output for re-review. <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/266">Orders chronology #266</a> has sufficient proof after fresh review, with owner approval reported for native newest-paid-first only; merge and API ordering remain separate. Green test suites, review-status checks, policy approval and signed deployment are separate.</p></details><table id="reports"><caption>Upstream reports · guest receipt identity checked November 16; other rows retain their dated evidence</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Report</th><th scope="col">Status &amp; store friction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-receipt-identity-report><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/283">Commerce #283 · Guest receipt identity</a></td><td>Open capability request, not a regression or release blocker. Signed 0.8 and source-built beta2 paid guest reads omit the canonical Orders number and test flag; read-only matching confirms the same numbered TEST order. Preserve cart-key authorization and frozen facts; no Commerce repair is implemented or deployed.</td></tr><tr data-feed-member-candidate><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/282">Commerce #282 · Concrete feed rows</a><br/><a href="https://github.com/saarius/commerce/tree/fix/variant-feed-rows">fix/variant-feed-rows · 07e68fe</a></td><td>Open source candidate with inline main/head CLI proof: eleven member rows, own effective money/stock, family grouping and host-supplied selected URLs. All 885 unit/workflow and 111 integration checks pass in isolated namespaces; source Registry backend is unchanged, and the signed live store still exports five simple shopping-feed rows.</td></tr><tr data-feed-member-report><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/281">Commerce #281 · Missing feed members</a></td><td>Open bug report, not an implemented repair: unchanged main b460433 and signed 0.8.0 both export five Google/Meta rows rather than eleven concrete members. The builder requires a root price that option families intentionally lack; member identity, effective money and availability must stay authoritative, separately from feed-control PR #280.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/235">Template #235 · Shared-session client repair</a><br/><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/shopper-session-tabs">fix/shopper-session-tabs · afe02f4</a></td><td>Open PR with generic unchanged-main/head public proof. Seventy-four focused desktop/phone cases, all unit/workflow gates and the Registry compile pass; the unrelated local admin welcome/heap failure also reproduces on main. Exact-head full CI passes; review pending. The matching merchant client mitigation already serves here, with no new signed plugin or business write.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/234">Template #234 · Shared shopper identity</a></td><td>Initial issue qualification, superseded by PR #235 above: an open report with a merchant mitigation, not an upstream PR or backend authorization change. Intercepted Account tabs sent A’s address using B’s newer shared session; the merchant client now clears old private views, refuses mismatched actions and ignores stale completions while preserving B. Sixty-two focused cases cover desktop/phone, Light/Dark, delayed responses and existing denial/transient recovery without real account writes. Compare <a href="/pr-proof/template-store-account-tabs/before-390.png">the stale phone view</a> and <a href="/pr-proof/template-store-account-tabs/after-390.png">the cleared view</a>; generic main/head proof and full owning verification remain prerequisites for a later PR.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/227#issuecomment-6881635674">Template #227 · Agent feed eligibility</a></td><td>Observed consequence of an explicit open decision, not a new defect or repair. The live JSON feed exports no products when all seven published families have empty Google/Meta channel eligibility. A local built Worker accepts the actual HTTPS feed; populated variant, effective-price and freshness checks use a separate synthetic fixture, not the shipping route. Merchant branch104dc5a adopts upstream23207d9; saarius/dinkuskit’s backroadbum/catalog-dogfood tracks catalog Worker662dd47 locally, with no shared deployment.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/276">Commerce #276 · Publishing after Restore</a></td><td>Open workflow report, not a repair. A disposable signed-Commerce0.8.0 copy restores a product as Draft while its CMS page remains live, leaving Save disabled and no Publish action; native unpublish → publish returns the same product and saved cart without changing paid Orders. Four redacted desktop/phone captures show <a href="/pr-proof/product-restore/restored-draft-390.png">the restored draft</a> and <a href="/pr-proof/product-restore/republished-390.png">the native workaround</a>; the accepted draft and single-page-publication contracts remain intact.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/229#issuecomment-6874204021">Template #229 · Blank update removes a line</a></td><td>Reported on the owning candidate. Empty quantity becomes zero in the server parser; populated carts became empty in four isolated desktop/phone script-on/off observations. Visible interaction proof is attached; no repair or merchant adoption is claimed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/275">Commerce #275 · Guest fulfillment visibility</a></td><td>Open capability request. The same completed TEST order has matching tracking in native and hosted Ship, while its original signed-Commerce guest receipt has no fulfillment, completion or status field. Read-only paid-order matching and an existing-label PDF check preserve original browser state and business records. Main 3f1ff30 and server-cart candidate #272 at a966e82 still project frozen checkout facts; any accepted guest read must use Orders’ later facts under its existing authority and coordinate with Template #229. No new contract, source patch, signed release or hosted deployment is claimed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/265">Commerce #265 · Finding recent orders</a></td><td>Closed by merged <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/266">PR #266</a> on November 13; the native-list source repair is accepted. The newest payment appears fifth in the signed eight-order list; the candidate sorts parsed payment time before pagination, with number/ID tie fallback and unknown legacy times last. Locally verified, not signed/deployed; #258’s scan cost and other consumers’ storage/API ordering stay separate.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/issues/123">DinkusKit #123 · Hosted store setup</a></td><td>Existing report, not opened by this cycle. A read-only owner visit confirmed the flat charge and next label share a line at 1440px and 390px; the field already has an accessible name but no visible associated label. <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/pull/124">PR #124</a> now reworks the existing card into owner-requested Plugins/Shipping/Payments links and independent native settings forms. The wider dashboard redesign remains open; no hosted settings or shared service changed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/264">Commerce #264 · Choices through packing</a></td><td>Closed November 13 after source repair <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/271">PR #271</a> merged at16:59. Owner-approved handoff sends frozen choices as one optional line per Ship item; Ship keeps/displays it, while simple products stay unchanged and existing test orders are not resynced. The signed store’s earlier M/L omission and untouched sender/receiver replay remain historical evidence, not proof of a new installed artifact or complete hosted rollout. No catalog inference, paid-money change, forced revision, resync or new label was made here; distinct from Orders #263, payment display #262 and missing-weight #97.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/224">template-store #224 · Inert buying controls</a></td><td>Earlier repair <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/225">PR #225</a> closed without merge on November 13; issue #224 stays open until the server-side cart build. Open <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/229">PR #229</a> contains the owner-locked server-cart/real-form implementation candidate, observed at 580a054 with open Commerce #272 at 1ef8465 on November 13 at 21:54 UTC. This late source observation is not an independent paired-runtime test or deployed fix; the author explicitly says not to merge it alone. Distinct from gallery #221. Without JavaScript, Add to cart did nothing and selecting sold-out XL retained the default member’s In stock status. Both candidates wait for bound handlers and explain the browser-cart requirement; only the merchant theme adds native GET option inspection through its existing selection URL. No no-script purchase or signed-plugin change is claimed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/payments/issues/118">Payments #118 · Retained checkout recovery</a></td><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/payments/issues/118#issuecomment-6870701600">Original attempts now release, verified November 14</a>. Public and signed native status reads return released-retry for the original $79 / $76 / $73 attempts; Commerce durably records expired-unpaid without an order. Four actual-store desktop/phone Light/Dark checks reach enabled checkout review after explicit status checks, retaining capability, attempt, cart and input files with no successor start. Merged <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/payments/pull/119">Payments #119</a> implements an explicit-null PaymentIntent expiry rule and size descriptions, but neither the precise provider objects nor deployed Worker revision was independently inspected here. The local sandbox credential cannot retrieve these connected-account Sessions; a scoped404 is not proof of absence. The issue remains open for that explanation, not a browser-reset workaround; no plugin or shared-service deployment was performed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/221">template-store #221 · Inert gallery buttons</a></td><td>Open report from attaching a second image through signed Commerce. Without JavaScript, thumbnail buttons looked actionable but could not show or open the detail view on desktop and phone. The <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/backroadbum/store">merchant theme</a> now renders every approved picture without gallery scripts or controls, following the owner’s revised desktop-grid/phone-snap direction. The separately verified generic rework is open as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/222">PR #222</a>; no release or shared deployment is claimed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/262">Commerce #262 · Selected sizes at payment</a></td><td>Closed November 13 after source repair <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/273">PR #273</a> merged at17:16. Owner-approved frozen choices now travel as payment-line descriptions; Payments uses them in Stripe while simple items omit descriptions and amounts, identities and frozen existing requests stay unchanged. The original M/L checkout showed identical lines despite correct Commerce identities; that remains the store evidence, not proof of an upgraded signed plugin or hosted deployment. No storefront-invented label, replacement checkout or new payment was made here.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/219">template-store #219 · Stale price on return</a></td><td>Closed by merged PR #220 on November 13; merchant repair deployed on <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/backroadbum/store">backroadbum/store</a>. Native sale editing exposed a retained cart that skipped its Commerce refresh when IDs and quantities were unchanged. Focus and restored-page refresh now preserve intent, invalid drafts and checkout fields; failed-write carts and active checkout attempts stay protected. Generic repair submitted as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/220">PR #220</a> at d8cde3a, with four controlled desktop/phone cart and checkout cases passing. No shared-service change or new payment is claimed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/issues/95">Ship #95 · Phone label history overflow</a></td><td>Closed November 13 on owner confirmation of merged source repair PR #96; observed through the signed plugin’s Open in Ship link on an existing TEST order. Hosted Labels is 531px wide on a 390px phone viewport and expands the page to 547px, moving print/cancel actions offscreen. The same page fits desktop; the existing label, PDF and canonical tracking are intact. Repair submitted as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/ship/pull/96">PR #96</a>; full local verification and owning GitHub tests pass. Actual served-route phone proof now fits 390px versus main’s synthetic 532px; the earlier hosted measurement remains separate, with no shared-service deployment claimed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/217">template-store #217 · Missing cart item names</a></td><td>Closed November 13 by merged <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/218">PR #218</a>; the merchant presentation repair was already deployed. <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/cart-fallback-labels">Fork candidate fix/cart-fallback-labels</a> is now at 3285ebc, with local deterministic, Registry and targeted desktop/phone proof; full GitHub desktop, phone, Registry and aggregate checks pass, and the generic fix is now merged upstream. Native unpublish/republish preserved the saved cart and correctly refused the missing product, but used its UUID as a heading and in Quantity/Remove names. Numbered fallback labels now distinguish missing rows without caching unpublished names or changing identities, quantities, prices or checkout decisions.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.c