efault/member HTTP output: family SKU unchanged, both member SKUs absent on main and distinct on the candidate, with unchanged storage. Fresh clean canonical builds and installed HTTP captures pass; standalone re-review was requested, and the owner has now approved the additive public contract. No production plugin replacement is deployed; template PR #214 consumes the optional field and safely handles older payloads.</DashboardEvidence></td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/invalid-cart-quantity">saarius/template-store · fix/invalid-cart-quantity</a></td><td><DashboardEvidence summary="Merged · #212 restores rejected quantity edits without another state store. Synthetic browser proof starts no payment.">Submitted as <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/212">PR #212</a> at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/823085f">823085f</a> for #211; merged upstream November 13 with CI green. Restores invalid edits without another state store or changes to Commerce. The browser regression uses synthetic catalog/checkout transport. Local typecheck, unit/workflow, targeted browser checks and credential-free Registry compilation passed. GitHub Actions also passed desktop, phone, Registry and aggregate verification; unrelated local baseline timeouts are documented in the PR. Four public Before/After composites now show actual Astro cart/checkout handlers at unchanged main 62949c8 and candidate 823085f on desktop and phone. Seven invalid inputs preserve storage and totals; rejected zero becomes 1/$24, and a rejected blank after a refused save becomes in-memory 2/$48 while persisted intent stays 3. All four flows per source pass their source-specific captures; the restoration comparison fails on main and passes on head, with no payment starts, errors or overflow. Fresh Node 24.22.0 typecheck, 578 units, 115 workflow passes, audits, Registry assertion and credential-free dry-run pass; the same-head owning test CI is green and one standalone re-review follows verified body/media publication. This synthetic catalog/admission protocol proves changed storefront behavior, not signed installation or provider readiness; the merchant’s different retained-draft repair is not used as proof.</DashboardEvidence></td></tr></tbody></table><table id="store-source"><caption>Store source and legacy work</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Status & purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/backroadbum/store">saarius/template-store · backroadbum/store</a></td><td>Branded storefront and public TEST checkout, durable request limits and non-creating readiness telemetry. Local Ship recovery now has online SQLite copies and an isolated restart drill. Visible product identifiers now follow the selected member’s optional public SKU and omit unknown identifiers rather than displaying a sibling’s; simple-product identifiers are unchanged. A disposable migration check now creates actual 0.8.0 kernel purchases and preserves their frozen facts through Commerce #272’s installed cart read; synthetic kernel replay is not hosted or signed proof. Fresh qualification at Commerce #272 head1ef8465 now includes the actual merchant wrapper: explicit cart-read mode returns the original paid receipt and unresolved attempt while refusing mutation bodies and other-attempt locators. The serving signed0.8.0 store keeps default legacy mode; no coordinated signed beta, Template #229 or hosted TEST migration is qualified here. Store-specific work, not an upstream proposal.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/saarius/payments/tree/backroadbum/test-runtime">saarius/payments · backroadbum/test-runtime</a></td><td>Retired Node host using v0.5.0 service ports, signed own-account events and durable wakes; service stopped/disabled and its old TEST webhook disabled. Data retained for recovery, not serving hosted Payments. Its merchan