  <section id="emdash-bugs"><h2>EmDash Bugs &amp; Friction (For Human Review)</h2><p><a href="/dashboard/emdash-bugs.txt">Versioned reproduction notes, root causes and workarounds</a>. This ledger separates observed sharp edges from confirmed CMS defects; reports to EmDash require human review.</p><ul><li>Standalone Node image transforms needed Sharp declared at the application root.</li><li>Untouched upstream admin/catalog seeding times out locally; cause remains unresolved.</li><li>Concurrent sandbox runners collide on the default workerd port in one network namespace.</li><li>Earlier deployments reached the 10-second stop timeout because runner cleanup left the application HTTP listener open. A merchant launcher now closes HTTP and drains accepted requests before releasing workerd, with eleven offline lifecycle checks and an isolated current-build comparison passing; initial activation was not a live shutdown test. The next normal stop at 22:24 UTC closed admission, drained and deactivated without a forced kill; samples began after restart and establish neither continuous uptime nor background-job drain. Missing encryption configuration is a separate, expected refusal. A November 15 disposable Astro dev fixture passed setup reads but hung during server.stop(); an unchanged bounded retry completed. That unresolved development-only shutdown edge is distinct from the serving launcher.</li><li>Block Kit Section text collapses newlines; Commerce’s order inspector needs separate wrapping rows. Expected host behavior, not a confirmed CMS defect; repair proposed in Commerce PR #261.</li><li>An automated keyboard reorder of expanded product-detail blocks stopped short; collapsing the blocks first allowed the desired order to save and reload. Cause remains unisolated from timing and scrolling, not a confirmed CMS defect.</li><li>A refused native weight form closes its Shipping disclosure while retaining input. A disposable replay isolates Commerce’s unkeyed-card state transfer; <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/267">PR #267</a> proposes stable Block Kit identities, without a CMS change. Reopen Shipping to correct in the unchanged signed plugin; this is not an assumed requirement for EmDash to reset local state.</li><li>At phone width, replacing the successfully saved weight form detaches its focused button; the resulting focus-leave event closes Kumo’s Settings sheet. An isolated installed replay reproduces click and keyboard Enter, while desktop retains its controls. Reopen Settings to read the saved value: both phone cases verify 12.5 oz without another save. <a href="/pr-proof/emdash-phone-settings/before-save-390.png">Before save</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/emdash-phone-settings/after-save-390.png">after save</a> show the interaction, not a fix. The owning repair remains for human review; invalid-save phone continuation is not qualified.</li><li>Search snippets select the title column even for body-text matches. Matching field notes now use a short published opening-paragraph preview when the snippet is absent or redundant; useful native snippets and result ranking stay unchanged. This is a discovery sharp edge with a merchant fallback, not a CMS patch or an upstream report.</li><li>The pinned native Blocks renderer exposes 16px-high accordion triggers and 18px-high switches in a synthetic product-panel mount, below the mobile 44px target. Commerce PR280 retains the host controls without CSS overrides; this is a versioned human-review observation, not a full native-editor audit or a fixed host defect.</li><li>The EmDash 1.4.0 playground toolbar exposes 22px and 20px buttons in the isolated server-cart fixture. Unfiltered reports retain those host findings; the clean merchant audit excludes only that toolbar and the separate tour, without claiming a CMS repair or live storefront defect.</li><li>Native Orders inspection removes its focused Inspect button and leaves BODY focused; reaching Back to orders then takes 32 desktop or five phone Tabs in the observed shell. Installed-source evidence and a synthetic pinned-renderer mirror isolate response replacement, without choosing a host/plugin focus policy or installing a repair. Use sequential Tab or pointer to Back; <a href="/pr-proof/emdash-order-focus/before-inspect-390.png">before inspection</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/emdash-order-focus/after-inspect-390.png">after inspection</a> contain synthetic facts only. Actual native Inspect targets are 36px high; the diagnostic preserves these host findings rather than applying merchant styles.</li><li>Missing block-type definitions in a disposable fixture cause one Pages field expansion to empty the entire admin manifest, while the schema API still lists all three collections. The operator copier now preserves these schema dependencies; the native price/stock workflow passes afterward. This is incomplete-fixture fallout plus a human-review failure-isolation observation, not a live-store defect or CMS patch.</li><li>EmDash 1.4.0 exports both a Portable Text type and the native component as Block; this merchant Astro consumer resolves the public name as type-only and rejects its use as a component. Using the public emdashComponents.block renderer with typed props passes the focused check and preserves native output. This is a human-review integration sharp edge, not a runtime failure or CMS patch.</li></ul></section><section id="costs"><h2>Activity & costs</h2>
    <p>Recorded metadata refreshes with telemetry, independently of agent cycles. Controller results and retained conversation records have different scopes: a missing final response is not evidence that a cycle failed.</p>
