  <section id="instructions"><h2>Owner instructions</h2><p>Instruction versions are kept in order without replacing earlier copies.</p><p>Steer 8 updates the working runtime and design skill and restores the hosted owner session. Steer 9 authorizes isolated dogfooding of the new Accounts and Reviews plugins. Neither is installed here: Accounts waits for its signed release paired with stable Commerce; Reviews waits for decided features and a signed release. Steer 10 adds Courier, the store-local event bus. The bootstrap and the starter’s Cloudflare timer have merged. Registry identity matching remains under investigation; the Cloudflare timer is not running on this Node store.</p><p>Steer 7 arrived November 20. A PR push starts its review automatically; do not queue a duplicate. Its narrow error/missing-pickup exceptions replace Steer 3’s older push-trigger instruction. No duplicate re-review trigger was posted during the November 22 follow-up; the execution timer remains operator-managed.</p><p>Steer 6 arrived November 15. It authorizes passive Google/Meta feed eligibility on the seven published products, without external enrollment, and isolated Commerce 0.9 beta server-cart qualification. Eligibility is enabled and the populated agent JSON is verified; XML/CSV variant coverage remains unfinished. Isolated source-built beta cart/recovery and Field Journal staging checks now pass, including an explicit earlier-checkout handoff with actual old-kernel disposable purchases; original live browsers, the complete regression matrix and signed merchant artifact qualification remain unfinished. The stable Registry still lists 0.8.0; the in-place live upgrade waits for stable 0.9.x under the existing plugin identity, a verified snapshot and the paired storefront. Neither track is claimed complete.</p><p>Steer 5 arrived November 14. The one-way upstream store sync and live agent-catalog route were completed first with a valid empty feed; Steer 6’s authorized eligibility change now supplies the populated JSON proof above. The native HTTPS transport now delivers real test mail and Commerce OTP to the verified sandbox inbox. A new TEST1010 purchase and the actual form journey now prove matching-order isolation, profile persistence and revocation. The account form is open with explicit verified-destination limits; unrestricted email delivery is not available on this plan.</p><ul><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/original-2026-11-09.txt">Original · captured November 9, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-1-2026-11-10.txt">Steer 1 · November 10, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-2-2026-11-11.txt">Steer 2 · November 11, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-3-2026-11-12.txt">Steer 3 · November 12, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-4-2026-11-13.txt">Steer 4 · November 13, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-5-2026-11-14.txt">Steer 5 · November 14, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-6-2026-11-15.txt">Steer 6 · November 15, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-7-2026-11-20.txt">Steer 7 · November 20, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-8-2026-11-22.txt">Steer 8 · November 22, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-9-2026-11-22.txt">Steer 9 · November 22, 2026</a></li><li><a href="/dashboard/instructions/steer-10-2026-11-22.txt">Steer 10 · November 22, 2026</a></li></ul></section>
